Both review axes found real improvements, especially on spec fidelity. I’m addressing them before finalizing:

- persist the selected-world capability database during the one-command fixture run;
- return node provenance and the traversed edge’s relation/provenance separately;
- add a two-edge cycle so removing the path guard would fail the test;
- remove the unsupported `--world` option and consolidate duplicated fixture/test setup.

These are review-stage corrections, as required by the TDD workflow.

